-- title:
--   Cyclotomic inertia forces finite-part points to reduce to one
-- statement:
--   Fix an odd prime $p$, a positive integer $M$ divisible by $p$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$, and a valuation subring $Pl$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ in its non-units, whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$; assume the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jqModC`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15) of $j$ lies in the field [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101). Given a model $\mathfrak{X}$ of type [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP`](def/ModularCurve_XHDRModelAtP.html#L81), level data $\Lambda$, a Néron object $O$ of type [`ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP`](def/ModularCurve_JHNeronObjectAtP.html#L53) (a smooth separated surjective group scheme $O.g : O.G \to \operatorname{Spec} R_p$ with relative group law $O.L$, whose points over the generic geometric fibre are identified with $J_H = \mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the level-$H$ function field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$), and a witness that the designation $(O.G, O.g, \text{identity section})$ represents the relative Picard functor of the two-chart integral model cut out by the fibrewise algebraic-equivalence-to-zero condition. Let $R$ be a henselian discrete valuation domain with algebraically closed residue field, mapping faithfully into $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with image inside $Pl$, in which $p$ is irreducible, such that an automorphism of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ lies in the inertia subgroup of $Pl$ exactly when it fixes the image of $R$ pointwise, and every inertia-fixed element of $Pl$ comes from $R$. Let $\mathcal{G}$ be a $p$-divisible group over $R$ of height $h$, and $\Delta$ an injective additive map from the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of $\mathcal{G}$ to $J_H(M,H)$ which, for each $v$, carries the level-$v$ points exactly onto $O.\mathrm{finPts}(p^v)$ — the subgroup generated by the $p^v$-torsion classes whose associated section extends over $Pl$ — and which is equivariant for automorphisms of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ over $R$ compared with their action on $J_H$. The conclusion: for every $x \in O.\mathrm{finPts}(p)$ such that for all $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup of $Pl$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and all $c \in \mathbb{N}$, $\sigma\zeta = \zeta^{c}$ for all $p$-th roots of unity $\zeta$ implies $\sigma \cdot x = c\,x$, there is a level-one point $y$ of $\mathcal{G}$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\Delta(y) = x$ and with $Pl$-valuation of $y(a) - \varepsilon(a)$ strictly less than $1$ for every $a$ in the level-one Hopf algebra $\mathcal{G}.\mathrm{level}\,1$, where $\varepsilon$ is the counit followed by $R \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; that is, $y$ reduces to the identity point.
--
--   This is the easy implication in the comparison of the connected and multiplicative parts of the $p$-divisible group attached to the Jacobian at $p$: a point of the finite part on which inertia acts through the mod-$p$ cyclotomic character reduces to the identity, the argument resting on the splitting of finite flat group schemes over the absolutely unramified base $R$ (where $e = 1 < p-1$). It is used by the corresponding equivalence at the ordinary corner, [`ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP.reducesToOne_iff_inertia_cyclotomic_of_mem_corner_of_mem_finPts_of_ordinary_of_abelJacobiPin_of_inertF_of_levelData_of_algEquiv`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP.reducesToOne_iff_inertia_cyclotomic_of_mem_corner_of_mem_finPts_of_ordinary_of_abelJacobiPin_of_inertF_of_levelData_of_algEquiv).
